[1] To make a particular user account usable only by WebSocket clients and not regular NATS connections, you need to configure the `allowed_connection_types` option under the `users` section in the authorization configuration. For example, to restrict user `bar` to accept only WebSocket clients, you would set the `allowed_connection_types` option as follows:

```json
authorization {
  users [ {
    user: bar,
    password: barpwd,
    permission: {...},
    allowed_connection_types: ["WEBSOCKET"]
  }]
}
```

This configuration ensures that the user `bar`, along with its password `barpwd`, can only authenticate using WebSocket connections, thus disallowing other types of connections such as standard NATS clients.
